 - The filePath parameter should be an absolute path.
 - By default, this tool returns up to 200 lines from the start of the file.
 - Text content is capped at 16 KiB per read; displayed lines are limited to 2000 characters. Use offset/limit to continue.
-- Line accounting scans at most 256 KiB beyond the returned page. If `<range total_exact="false">` appears, `total` is a lower bound; otherwise it is exact.
+- The tool may inspect up to 256 KB of additional text plus one 16 KB read-ahead chunk to estimate line totals on a large remainder; this input is not returned as content.
+- The `total` attribute is exact when line accounting reaches EOF; `total_exact="false"` marks a bounded-scan lower bound, always at least one line beyond the returned range.
+- The `<more>` element means unread file content remains. It can be present even when `total` is exact.
 - The offset parameter is the line number to start from (1-indexed).
 - To read later sections, call this tool again with a larger offset.
 - Use the grep tool to find specific content in large files or files with long lines.

